  "question": {
    "text": "<strong>Paragraph:</strong>\nThe nuclear charge $(\\mathrm{Ze})$ is non-uniformly distributed within a nucleus of radius $R$. The charge density $\\rho(r)$ [charge per unit volume] is dependent only on the radial distance $r$ from the centre of the nucleus as shown in figure. The electric field is only along the radial direction.<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/jlFKxAkJt_03DKXWqhIFlKSRLGpw3OZjlz0a8gNGa4M.original.fullsize.png\"><br><strong>Question:</strong>\nThe electric field at $r=R$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "jHkPJ",
      "text": "\nindependent of $a$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "q19NP",
      "text": "\ndirectly proportional to $a$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Fw8OM",
      "text": "\ndirectly proportional to $a^2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "6IZYV",
      "text": "\ninversely proportional to $a$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "At $r=R$, from Gauss's law\nor\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE\\left(4 \\pi R^2\\right) & =\\frac{q_{\\text {net }}}{\\varepsilon_0}=\\frac{Z e}{\\varepsilon_0} \\\\\nE & =\\frac{1}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_0} \\cdot \\frac{Z e}{R^2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n$E$ is independent of ' $a$ '\n$\\therefore$ correct option is (a).",
    "image": null
  },
